Draft from the context itself when the last step was fully accepted.

A request that is reproducing its prompt (quoting a document, applying an edit)
has its continuation already in the token history. This builds that history from
the authoritative `sampled_token_ids` (the CPU copy lags a token), matches the
tail with a suffix lookup, and hands the match to the sampler as a whole-block
draft, with no model calls at all.

Greedy only by default, gated by `VLLM_MTP_LOOKUP` and `VLLM_MTP_LOOKUP_MIN`.
`VLLM_MTP_LOOKUP_SAMPLED=1` opts sampled traffic in as well. The proposal is
still exact there (a point mass is a legal q for the rejection sampler, with
acceptance p(x) per position), but it is a *weaker* draft than the drafter's
own distribution wherever the drafter is right: measured on 23k-token
documents at temperature 1.0, copy +17% and quote +13% decode, but free-form
summary -9.5%. `LOOKUP_MIN` cannot exceed `NMAX`; raising both (`NMAX=64`,
`MIN=48`, `NMIN=8`) buys quote (+27%) and edit (+3.5%) as well and still
loses ~7% on prose. DFlash2 fuses the two proposals to avoid this, but the
fusion does not port cleanly: the MTP drafter sees the whole context, so on
copy work the lookup's value comes precisely from disagreeing with it. Keep
sampled lookup opt-in, with the NMAX=64 gate for copy-heavy traffic.
`NMIN`/`NMAX`/`SEARCH` bound the search.

